Supply-Chain Diversification Is Reshaping Production

The electronics manufacturing ecosystem is geographically concentrated, but customers increasingly evaluate sourcing resilience and alternative production locations. ODMs and EMS providers must balance labor availability, logistics, supplier access, infrastructure, regulatory considerations and manufacturing costs.

Production diversification can improve supply-chain flexibility, but establishing new facilities and qualifying suppliers requires investment and time. Consistent quality across multiple locations is also essential.

